ectar_santorini and @blusantorini . Job requirements: Previous experience in a similar position, ideally in a hotel environment. Physical endurance and responsibility. Attention to detail and speed of execution. Team spirit and positive attitude. Job responsibilities: Cleaning and tidying up indoor areas & outdoor areas. Replenishment of consumables (paper, soaps, perfumes). Informing the supervisor of damage, shortages or unusual incidents. Cleaning restaurants /seat covers/ pool areas/ sunbed covers. Participation in general cleaning (deep cleaning). Preparation and provision of cleaning supplies e.g. Medicines, cloths, etc. Cleaning and tidying up cleaning tools. Tidying up items not used at the end of the shift. Following instructions and adhering to a timeframe and cleaning sequence. Adhering to safety and hygiene rules. Professional appearance and discretion. Job Benefits: Tailored Compensation | Salary package customized to fairly reflect your profile and expertise. Staff Residences | Shared accommodations of up to 2 pax, with comfort amenities, ensuring a seamless home-away-from-home experience in Santorini. All-day Meal Plan | Balanced and freshly prepared meals (breakfast, lunch, dinner), served in welcoming staff dining setting. Exclusive Staff Privileges | Access to special staff discounts across our network of partners and Friends & Family rates for your loved ones. Pathway to Growth & Development | Ongoing professional development in line with global hospitality standards and a clear trajectory for career advancement within a fast-growing, award-winning resort. Recognition & Rewards | Access to bonus schemes and recognition initiatives that celebrate talent, achievement, and contribution to the Sandblu vision, along with CSR and engagement activities that foster connection and purpose. Passion, precision, purpose – make this your own career story. We are a team of passionate, creative professionals delivering heartfelt hospitality, where precision, warmth, and artistry define every interaction. We nurture growth, celebrate individuality, and empower our team to thrive in a culture built on collaboration and shared purpose. Your Worklife at Sandblu: Warmth & Unforgettable Hospitality | Teamwork & Positive Energy | Kindness, Empathy, Integrity | Continuous Improvement | Learning Something New Every Day At Sandblu, our teams are at the heart of every guest experience, embodying the spirit and values of our brand, as true ambassadors. Every element of the employee experience reflects the same attention to detail we offer to our guests. We are actively committed to their well-being, from modern accommodations and nutritious meals to a balanced, fulfilling and friendly work environment, where respect is protected. We open pathways for their growth and recognize their contributions, empowering them with every tool to make an impact at their job from day one, so they can bring their best selves to work every day. If you are driven to create extraordinary experiences and make an impact from day one, click on the \"Application\" tab to Apply! RMKA PC and RSTQ PC are equal opportunity employers. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, or age.', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(773479, 'Bell Attendant', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kn903t30qp47ywppm6mwrbkz/bell-attendant', 'n/a', '2026-04-03', '2026-04-03 08:00:24', 'SANDBLU', 'Sandblu Resort is currently in search of: Bell Attendant Sandblu: Shaping a new era of ultra-luxury hospitality in Santorini Perched on the foothills of Ancient Thira, Sandblu redefines world-class luxury on the island of Santorini. Since first opening its doors in 2024, the resort has earned recognition among hundreds of guests 5-star reviews but also prestigious Media including Vogue, Travel & Leisure, Condé Nast Traveler, The Times, Robb Report and more. In 2025, we proudly launched Blu Restaurant in Imerovigli, extending the Caldera Experience, and received “Greece’s Best Hotel Restaurant 2025” award for Nectar at the World Culinary Awards. With 66 exquisitely designed accommodation options, multiple exceptional dining venues, Aurora Spa, Nous & Soma Fitness Center, a kids’ club, several retail boutiques, a chapel and multi-purpose areas for bespoke events, Sandblu offers a complete, full-service 5-star resort experience, in a Cycladic village setting. From wellness retreats to one-of-a-kind in-house experiences for guests, every moment spent here is thoughtfully curated and made to be remembered. As a fast-growing, award-winning company with headquarters in Athens, Sandblu partners with leading consortia, participates in international trade shows and fairs, and innovates towards a vision for building microcosm of extraordinary experiences across Santorini, with respect to the heritage and the local community. With a growth mindset and a commitment to excellence and constant improvement, Sandblu offers it all. It’s a flagship destination where every detail is intentional, and every guest journey unforgettable. Discover more: Sandblu Restaurant Gallery, Nectar Restaurant Gallery and Blu Restaurant Gallery or find us on social media at Sandblu, Nectar Restaurant and Blu Restaurant. Job requirements: Experience in luxury hotel or guest-facing role. Strong guest service, clear communication, and problem-solving skills. English fluency, Greek preferred (additional languages a plus). Valid driving license, safe, confident buggy/vehicle handling. Organized and detail-oriented personality. Impeccable grooming and professional, courteous manner. Flexibility for rotating shifts, weekends, and holidays. Job responsibilities: Receive clear handovers and review pending issues, note open items for the next shift. Replenish stations and ensure readiness for current and next shift. Check daily hotel status and support with timely luggage assistance for check ins, check outs and general transportation on premises. Maintain cleanliness and order of the entrance and luggage room, complete required checklists. Check buggies are recharged and washed as needed, report maintenance issues. Deliver newspapers/envelopes to rooms when required. Check politely with guests at the entrance and ensure your presence is always at the gate for a warm welcome. Escalate maintenance, safety, or guest issues promptly to the Concierge/Front Office leadership. Job benefits: Tailored Compensation: Salary package customized to fairly reflect your profile and expertise. Staff Residences: Shared accommodations of up to 2 pax, with comfort amenities, ensuring a seamless home-away-from-home experience in Santorini. All-day Meal Plan: Balanced and freshly prepared meals (breakfast, lunch, dinner), served in welcoming staff dining setting. Exclusive Staff Privileges: Access to special staff discounts across our network of partners and Friends & Family rates for your loved ones. Pathway to Growth & Development: Ongoing professional development in line with global hospitality standards and a clear trajectory for career advancement within a fast-growing, award-winning resort. Recognition & Rewards: Access to performance-based bonus schemes and recognition initiatives that celebrate talent, achievement, and contribution to the Sandblu vision, along with CSR and engagement activities that foster connection and purpose. Passion, precision, purpose – make this your own career story.   We are a team of passionate, creative professionals delivering heartfelt hospitality, where precision, warmth, and artistry define every interaction. We nurture growth, celebrate individuality, and empower our team to thrive in a culture built on collaboration and shared purpose. Your Worklife at Sandblu  Warmth & Unforgettable Hospitality | Teamwork & Positive Energy | Kindness, Empathy, Integrity | Continuous Improvement | Learning Something New Every Day. At Sandblu, our teams are at the heart of every guest experience, embodying the spirit and values of our brand, as true ambassadors. Every element of the employee experience reflects the same attention to detail we offer to our guests. We are actively committed to their well-being, from modern accommodations and nutritious meals to a balanced, fulfilling and friendly work environment, where respect is protected. We open pathways for their growth and recognize their contributions, empowering them with every tool to make an impact at their job from day one, so they can bring their best selves to work every day.  If you are driven to create extraordinary experiences and make an impact from day one, click on the \"Application\" tab to Apply! RMKA PC and RSTQ PC are equal opportunity employers. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, or age. ', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(773480, 'Hostess', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kn904n3wnafezj83k49tafkt/hostess', 'n/a', '2026-04-03', '2026-04-03 08:00:24', 'SANDBLU', 'Luxury, thoughtfully curated. Extended on the foothills of Ancient Thira, Sandblu Santorini redefines luxury through thoughtfully curated experiences. Our rooms, suites, and villas showcase a bright, naturally refined aesthetic, delivering the ultimate in luxury. Upon arrival, guests enter a world of sophistication and comfort, with breathtaking views of the Aegean Sea. The resort offers 66 elegantly appointed rooms, seven dining outlets, Aurora Spa, the Nous & Soma fitness center, the Bala kids\' club, retail stores, and a chapel for bespoke weddings and events.  At Sandblu Resort Santorini, we are a community of passionate and creative individuals dedicated to making a difference. We value our motivated team, providing them with invaluable support and leadership. Every team member contributes unique skills, experiences, and viewpoints, all of which are vital to the dynamic and rewarding atmosphere that sets our workplace apart. We are looking forward to connecting with professionals ready to grow with us.  As part of our growing hospitality ventures, Sandblu is proud to introduce Blu Restaurant, our signature gastronomic destination perched on the caldera cliffs of Imerovigli. Blu is where the essence of the Aegean meets global culinary explorations. Deeply rooted in the soul of Sandblu and designed by the renowned Rockwell Group, Blu transforms our philosophy into a sensory dining experience, bringing the same spirit of “quiet luxury” to a setting framed by panoramic caldera views, refined fusion cuisine, and soulful ambiance. Together, they form a seamless microcosmos of elevated hospitality, where every detail is intentional, and every moment is designed to be felt. Joining Sandblu means more than joining a team; it means shaping the standards of hospitality from your very first day. We approach every moment with intention, blending precision with genuine warmth, and expertise with artistry. Each experience we offer to our guests is crafted to be intuitive, tailored, and unforgettable, because we believe that true luxury is found in authenticity, and our teams’ unique passion and commitment. Sandblu Resort is currently in search of Host Duties and Responsibilities: Greet all guests warmly and professionally upon arrival, using their names when known. Manage table reservations and walk-ins efficiently using the restaurant’s booking system. Escort guests to their tables and present menus with elegance and confidence. Maintain a polished, elegant, and approachable appearance at all times. Provide accurate wait time estimates during busy periods and manage guest expectations. Liaise effectively with the service team to ensure a smooth flow of operations. Keep the reception and entrance area clean, organized, and welcoming. Handle guest inquiries and complaints gracefully, escalating to management when necessary. Be fully informed of daily specials, events, and VIP guest arrivals. Assist with cloakroom service, special occasion setups, or personalized guest touches as needed. Ensure a luxurious and consistent guest experience aligned with SANDBLU standards. Participate in daily briefings and trainings to stay aligned with service excellence goals. Uphold health, safety, and hygiene standards at all times. Qualifications/Experience: Previous experience in a similar role within a luxury hotel or fine dining restaurant is essential (minimum 1-2 years). Excellent command of English (spoken and written); knowledge of additional languages is a strong asset. Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills Ability to remain calm, polite, and efficient under pressure. Team-oriented mindset with a guest-first attitude Flexibility to work evening shifts, weekends, and holidays. Passion for hospitality, attention to detail, and genuine interest in creating memorable guest experiences. Benefits: Learning & Development Program Dynamic and highly professional environment Career growth opportunities Accommodation and meals provided (in Santorini) If you are ready to join a team that values excellence, creativity, and collaboration, we would love to hear from you! RMKA IKE is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, or age. Discover more at www.sandblu.com or @sandblu on Instagram and Facebook', 'Με φυσική παρουσία'),
(773481, 'Guest Relations / Ambassador', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kn901e64p1mackd9bhre0jzk/guest-relations---ambassador', 'n/a', '2026-04-03', '2026-04-03 08:00:26', 'SANDBLU', 'Sandblu Resort is currently in search of: Guest Relations / Ambassador Sandblu: Shaping a new era of ultra-luxury hospitality in Santorini Perched on the foothills of Ancient Thira, Sandblu redefines world-class luxury on the island of Santorini. Since first opening its doors in 2024, the resort has earned recognition among hundreds of guests 5-star reviews but also prestigious Media including Vogue, Travel & Leisure, Condé Nast Traveler, The Times, Robb Report and more. In 2025, we proudly launched Blu Restaurant in Imerovigli, extending the Caldera Experience, and received “Greece’s Best Hotel Restaurant 2025” award for Nectar at the World Culinary Awards. With 66 exquisitely designed accommodation options, multiple exceptional dining venues, Aurora Spa, Nous & Soma Fitness Center, a kids’ club, several retail boutiques, a chapel and multi-purpose areas for bespoke events, Sandblu offers a complete, full-service 5-star resort experience, in a Cycladic village setting. From wellness retreats to one-of-a-kind in-house experiences for guests, every moment spent here is thoughtfully curated and made to be remembered. As a fast-growing, award-winning company with headquarters in Athens, Sandblu partners with leading consortia, participates in international trade shows and fairs, and innovates towards a vision for building microcosm of extraordinary experiences across Santorini, with respect to the heritage and the local community. With a growth mindset and a commitment to excellence and constant improvement, Sandblu offers it all. It’s a flagship destination where every detail is intentional, and every guest journey unforgettable. Discover more:  sandblu.com/gallery, nectarsantorini.com/gallery and blusantorini.com/gallery or find us on social media at @sandbluresort , @nectar_santorini and @blusantorini . Duties & responsibilities Shift Prep: check/reply to emails, review Night/FO handover, print Arrival & In‑House lists, note pending incidents, learn weekly activities (carry a hard copy). Lobby Standards: ensure lobby/public areas are tidy, clean, and well‑maintained; confirm lavettes are stocked for arrivals. Breakfast & Lunch Runs: meet & greet at Plateia, pool bars, and restaurants; check satisfaction, assist promptly, and cross‑sell on‑property outlets. Meet & Greet Etiquette: apply the 10–5 rule, use guest names, remain visible, and engage proactively. Personalized Service: discover preferences/needs, coordinate welcome drinks with F&B, and escort or direct guests to rooms. Groups & Queues: support group check‑ins/outs to keep the flow smooth and prevent queues. Issue Resolution: handle guest issues end‑to‑end and follow up personally to confirm satisfaction. Records & Feedback: update profiles/preferences; add comments to the Feedback report, re‑engage happy guests and politely encourage reviews. Courtesy Calls (17:30–19:00): confirm room satisfaction, offer assistance, suggest dining/activities, and share direct contact details. Dinner Run (19:30–20:30): meet & greet in restaurants; check satisfaction and assist as needed. Events Support: greet and guide group attendees to banquet/event spaces. End‑of‑Shift Handover: record open items and expectations; brief and note remarks for the next shift. Qualifications/experience At least 2 years in luxury hospitality or a guest‑facing role. Excellent communication with warm, confident guest interaction. Fluent English, Greek preferred (additional languages a plus). Strong problem‑solving and service recovery skills. Organized, proactive, and comfortable in busy lobby environments. Tech‑savvy, able to log preferences/notes in PMS/CRM (e.g. Opera). Impeccable grooming and professional presence. Flexibility for rotating shifts, weekends and knowledge of Santorini is a plus. What awaits you at sandblu: Tailored Compensation | Salary package customized to fairly reflect your profile and expertise. Staff Residences | Shared accommodations of up to 2 pax, with comfort amenities, ensuring a seamless home-away-from-home experience in Santorini. All-day Meal Plan | Balanced and freshly prepared meals (breakfast, lunch, dinner), served in welcoming staff dining setting. Exclusive Staff Privileges | Access to special staff discounts across our network of partners and Friends & Family rates for your loved ones. Pathway to Growth & Development | Ongoing professional development in line with global hospitality standards and a clear trajectory for career advancement within a fast-growing, award-winning resort. Recognition & Rewards | Access to bonus schemes and recognition initiatives that celebrate talent, achievement, and contribution to the Sandblu vision, along with CSR and engagement activities that foster connection and purpose. Passion, precision, purpose – make this your own career story. We are a team of passionate, creative professionals delivering heartfelt hospitality, where precision, warmth, and artistry define every interaction. We nurture growth, celebrate individuality, and empower our team to thrive in a culture built on collaboration and shared purpose. Your Worklife at Sandblu Warmth & Unforgettable Hospitality | Teamwork & Positive Energy | Kindness, Empathy, Integrity | Continuous Improvement | Learning Something New Every Day At Sandblu, our teams are at the heart of every guest experience, embodying the spirit and values of our brand, as true ambassadors. Every element of the employee experience reflects the same attention to detail we offer to our guests. We are actively committed to their well-being, from modern accommodations and nutritious meals to a balanced, fulfilling and friendly work environment, where respect is protected. We open pathways for their growth and recognize their contributions, empowering them with every tool to make an impact at their job from day one, so they can bring their best selves to work every day. If you are driven to create extraordinary experiences and make an impact from day one, send us your CV RMKA PC and RSTQ PC are equal opportunity employers. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, or age.', 'Με φυσική παρουσία'),
