(784970, 'Chef De Partie (Α\' Μάγειρας)', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvvjj8vy27zn46fx7d360g/chef-de-partie--a--mageiras-', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:40', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Chef De Partie to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Chef De Partie carries out kitchen duties whilst ensuring smooth, coordinated team effort in the kitchen. The Chef De Partie reports to the Junior Sous Chef. As Chef De Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Work closely with the Culinary team on daily operations and food quality control. Ensure proper food handling, monitor raw food availability, and inspect incoming goods. Attend all training sessions and participate in special events, promotions, and demonstrations. Maintain a clean, presentable uniform and ensure personal hygiene. Inform the Executive Chef and Chef de Cuisine regarding operational issues. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Chef De Partie, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 3 years of culinary experience. Good level in English or Greek.  Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Με φυσική παρουσία'),
(784971, 'Digital Marketing Technical Specialist - Heraklion, Crete', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvvah26sn786mt025n2tyw/digital-marketing-technical-specialist---heraklion--crete', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:40', 'METAXA HOSPITALITY GROUP', 'Metaxa Hospitality Group, awarded as the \"Best Hospitality Group in Greece\" by the World Travel Awards 2021 - 2025, has been creating unique experiences of authentic hospitality for more than five decades and invites you to become a member of a group of multi-awarded in Crete and Santorini. Metaxa Hospitality Group is looking for its Sales & Marketing Department based in Heraklion: Digital Marketing Technical Specialist We are seeking a Digital Marketing Technical Specialist to support the technical foundation of our digital marketing activities with a strong focus on Technical SEO/GEO, tracking, and website performance. The role is responsible for ensuring the accuracy of data, the reliability of tracking, and the overall health and performance of our digital platforms, enabling effective optimization and informed decision-making. You will contribute to the continuous improvement of our digital ecosystem, ensuring that systems, tools, and platforms operate efficiently and support performance growth across all channels. Key Responsibilities Technical SEO / GEO: Support the implementation and ongoing optimization of Technical SEO and GEO initiatives Monitor website health, indexation, crawlability, and overall search performance Support structured data implementation and ensure consistency across search and entity signals Identify and resolve technical issues impacting organic visibility Tracking & Analytics: Implement and maintain tracking through tag management systems Configure and validate events within analytics platforms Ensure accurate conversion tracking and data consistency across all digital channels Identify and resolve tracking or attribution issues Campaign Technical Support: Support campaign implementation from a technical perspective, including tracking setup, validation, and data integrity Ensure correct data flow between platforms and reporting systems Website Performance & Optimization: Manage website updates and support UX and conversion-focused improvements Perform minor front-end adjustments (content updates, layout fixes, basic styling) Monitor website performance and troubleshoot technical issues Data & Reporting Support: Support the development and maintenance of reporting dashboards Monitor data accuracy and identify discrepancies across platforms Marketing Technology & Integrations: Support the implementation and maintenance of marketing tools and integrations Manage tracking scripts, pixels, and platform connections Ensure systems operate efficiently across the digital ecosystem Optimization Support: Identify technical and data-driven opportunities to support continuous optimization of website performance, user journeys, and digital channels Necessary qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related field 2–4 years of experience in a digital marketing, analytics, or web-related technical role Hands-on experience with tag management systems and web analytics platforms (e.g., GTM, GA4 or similar) Experience working with website structures and managing technical updates Good understanding of Technical SEO principles (indexation, crawlability, site structure, performance) Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Understanding of how digital marketing platforms, tracking, and data flows interact Desired qualifications: Basic front-end knowledge (HTML, CSS, basic JavaScript) for minor website adjustments Experience with SEO tools (e.g., Search Console, crawling tools, or similar) Familiarity with reporting/dashboard tools (e.g., Looker Studio or similar) Experience working with third-party platforms (e.g., booking engines, affiliate platforms, or similar environments) Exposure to marketing technology tools and integrations Soft Skills High attention to detail and data accuracy Structured and methodical approach to problem-solving Ability to work independently and take ownership of technical areas Strong communication skills to collaborate effectively with internal teams and external partners Proactive mindset with the ability to identify and address issues We offer: Competitive salary remuneration Career development in a fast-paced, growing work environment. Training opportunities. Full year job Friendly work environment', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(784972, 'Sous Chef', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvrjs1cy5ynad9hstfd02a/sous-chef', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:42', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a  Sous Chef to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job: Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Sous Chef ensures the smooth running of the operations and the good working environment between colleagues. The Sous Chef reports to the Chef de Cuisine. As Sous Chef, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Check the quality of all food production in the kitchen, ensure all live products received are in top condition and are of top quality, oversee stock rotation (F.I.F.O.) and carry out the kitchen requisitioning and ordering. Check standard recipes ensuring proper portion control and uniformity of taste and quality. Oversee the overall food cost, as well as kitchen supplies, kitchen energy costs and kitchen utensils. Propose, and initiate when approved, new services and products for our guests. Motivate and lead by example. Ensure that all designated action points from daily briefings or other operational meetings are being followed by the individuals concerned. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Sous Chef, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 2 years of experience in a similar role. Fluency in English.  Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784973, 'Junior Sous Chef', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvs3jjz6w007pmt60vpj94/junior-sous-chef', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:42', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Junior Sous Chef to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Junior Sous Chef ensures the smooth running of culinary operations and the good working environment between colleagues. The Junior Sous Chef reports to the Sous Chef.  As Junior Sous Chef, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Check the quality of all food production in the kitchen, ensure all live products received are in top condition and are of top quality, oversee stock rotation (F.I.F.O.) and carry out the kitchen requisitioning and ordering. Check standard recipes ensuring proper portion control and uniformity of taste and quality. Oversee the overall food cost, as well as kitchen supplies, kitchen energy costs and kitchen utensils. Propose, and initiate when approved, new services and products for our guests. Motivate and lead by example. Ensure that all designated action points from daily briefings or other operational meetings are being followed by the individuals concerned. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Junior Sous Chef, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 1-2 years of experience in a similar role. Good level in English.  Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784974, 'Προγραμματιστές - Θεσσαλονίκη', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvs9wkcmaf4w391wg7mmmz/programmatistes---thessaloniki', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:44', 'Μονάδα Ψηφιακής Διακυβέρνησης ΑΠΘ', 'Μονάδα Ψηφιακής Διακυβέρνησης  Αριστοτέλειο Πανεπιστήμιο Θεσσαλονίκης Προγραμματιστές H Μονάδα Ψηφιακής Διακυβέρνησης ΑΠΘ   παρέχει μια πληθώρα υπηρεσιών διασφαλίζοντας την εύρυθμη λειτουργία και αναβάθμιση των δικτυακών και υπολογιστικών υποδομών του Ιδρύματος. Στελεχώνεται από μηχανικούς και επιστήμονες πληροφορικής όλων των ειδικοτήτων, καλύπτοντας όλο το φάσμα των δραστηριοτήτων ΤΠΕ, από τη διαχείριση υποδομών δικτύων και datacenters, μέχρι την ανάπτυξη και διαχείριση εφαρμογών, αναπτύσσοντας ψηφιακές υπηρεσίες που εξυπηρετούν την πανεπιστημιακή κοινότητα. Στο πλαίσιο του παραδοτέου για την Πλήρη Εφαρμογή της Στρατηγικής διασφάλισης ποιότητας του έργου «Μονάδα Διασφάλισης Ποιότητας », η Μονάδα Ψηφιακής Διακυβέρνησης αναζητά Προγραμματιστές (developers). Συγκεκριμένα στο πλαίσιο του έργου, πρόκειται να απασχοληθούν στελέχη ΠΕ Θετικών Επιστημών, Πληροφορικής ή Ηλεκτρολόγων Μηχανικών & Μηχανικών Υπολογιστών ή συναφών Τμημάτων έως 30/11/2027. Πληροφορίες για τη διαδικασία υποβολής αίτησης και δικαιολογητικών: https://it.auth.gr/announcements/anazitisi-developers/ Προθεσμία υποβολής: 11/05/2026 κα ώρα 14:00', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(784975, 'Σερβιτόρος Α\' & Β\' - Κρήτη', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvscczkfxwzd2mrva7m9qq/servitoros-a----v----kriti', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:44', 'AQUILA HOTELS & RESORTS', 'Η Aquila Hotels & Resorts είναι ένας από τους πλέον καινοτόμους ξενοδοχειακούς ομίλους της Κρήτης – διαθέτοντας τέσσερις από τις πιο διάσημες μονάδες 5* του νησιού. Η φιλοξενία είναι για εμάς τρόπος ζωής και η πολυτέλεια, το πάθος μας. Η έμπειρη ομάδα καταρτισμένου ανθρώπινου δυναμικού με πολυετή εμπειρία στον κλάδο είναι το στοιχείο που μας φέρνει στην κορυφή. Στόχος μας είναι να εμπλουτίσουμε την ομάδα του εκάστοτε ξενοδοχείου με νέους επαγγελματίες, που επιθυμούν να αναδειχθούν στον συναρπαστικό κόσμο του τουρισμού. Στείλε μας το βιογραφικό σου και κάνε την αίτησή σου τώρα για την παρακάτω θέση: Σερβιτόρος Α\' & Β\' Απαιτούμενα προσόντα: Γνώσεις εστιατορικής τέχνης Εμπειρία σε αντίστοιχη ή παρεμφερή θέση Πολύ καλή γνώση της αγγλικής γλώσσας (επιθυμητή η γνώση της γερμανικής γλώσσας) Διαπροσωπικές και επικοινωνιακές ικανότητες Επαγγελματική συμπεριφορά και φιλική προσωπικότητα Πνεύμα συνεργασίας και ομαδικότητας Να διακατέχεται από συνέπεια και αποτελεσματικότητα Γνώσεις διαδικασιών υγιεινής, ασφάλειας και διαχείρισης τροφίμων και ποτών Εστίαση στην παροχή υπηρεσιών υψηλού επιπέδου Παροχές: Ευχάριστο περιβάλλον εργασίας Συνεχής επιμόρφωση στις νέες τάσεις της τουριστικής αγοράς Ελκυστικό πακέτο αποδοχών και προοπτικές επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης Δυνατότητα διαμονής Επισκεφτείτε την ιστοσελίδα μας: www.aquilahotels.com και στο πεδίο «Καριέρα» συμπληρώστε την ηλεκτρονική φόρμα επισυνάπτοντας το βιογραφικό σας.', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784976, 'Digital Marketing Assistant– Heraklion, Crete', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvqv9v6v8cy0pmd627jqdr/digital-marketing-assistant%E2%80%93-heraklion--crete', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:46', 'METAXA HOSPITALITY GROUP', 'Metaxa Hospitality Group, awarded as the \"Best Hospitality Group in Greece\" by the World Travel Awards 2021 - 2025, has been creating unique experiences of authentic hospitality for more than five decades and invites you to become a member of a group of multi-awarded in Crete and Santorini. Metaxa Hospitality Group is looking for its Sales & Marketing Department based in Heraklion: Digital Marketing Assistant We are seeking a Digital Marketing Assistant to support the execution and day-to-day management of our digital marketing activities across the Group’s portfolio. The role will focus on campaign support, reporting, and operational coordination, contributing to the effectiveness and consistency of our digital presence. Key Responsibilities Campaign Execution Support: Assist in the setup and implementation of digital campaigns across platforms (Google Ads, Meta Ads) Upload and manage campaign assets, ensuring accuracy and alignment with campaign requirements Perform quality checks before and during campaign launches Performance Monitoring & Reporting: Monitor campaign performance on a daily basis and highlight any irregularities or optimization opportunities Prepare recurring reports and support the analysis of campaign performance Ensure accuracy and consistency of reported data Collaboration & Content Coordination: Work closely with the Copywriter and Art Director to support the development of cohesive and effective marketing campaigns Ensure alignment between campaign requirements and delivered creative assets across channels Operational & Coordination Support: Maintain internal documentation and campaign structures Support coordination between Digital Marketing, other internal teams, and external collaborators Necessary qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related field Basic understanding of paid media platforms (Google Ads and/or Meta Ads) Knowledge of Social Media Marketing and social media management Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and familiarity with Microsoft 365 tools Very good knowledge of the English language (both written and spoken) Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Ability to manage multiple tasks in a structured and timely manner Desired qualifications: 1–2 years of experience in digital marketing or a related field, ideally within the hospitality or tourism sector Familiarity with Google Ads and Meta Ads platforms Basic knowledge of Google Analytics Soft Skills: Proactive with a willingness to learn and develop Detail-oriented with a structured approach to execution Strong team collaboration and communication skills Ability to follow processes and ensure consistency We offer: Competitive salary remuneration Career development in a fast-paced, growing work environment. Training opportunities. Full year job Friendly work environment', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(784977, 'F&B Supervisor', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvqj5rjcv8ym4p6yyaszne/f-b-supervisor', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:46', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an F&B Supervisor to join our Food & Beverage Team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the F&B Supervisor provides efficient and friendly service, ensuring guests and residents satisfaction is achieved throughout their experience, whilst also providing the team with support. The F&B Supervisor reports to the Assistant Restaurant Manager. As F&B Supervisor, you will be responsible for the following duties: Oversee and manage shifts effectively to ensure a smooth and effective overall operation, by guiding colleagues on and by personally involving himself/herself in all aspects of the sequence of service. Provide direction and support to all outlet colleagues at any time, particularly during the operational hours. Support the management team when required to train colleagues, in accordance with the applicable standards and policies. Follow the side duty schedule and assure all tasks are completed at all times in a timely manner. Assure the back and front of house areas of the outlet are clean and tidy at all times. Identify areas for improvement in F&B service and quality, through guest comments, comment cards and guest incident reports, and share observations and recommendations with the management team. As F&B Supervisor, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit 2 years\' experience in a similar role, in a luxury hotel operation Fluency in English Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant Uniform and laundry of uniform Private Medical Insurance We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784978, 'Barista - Πωλητής - Σαντορίνη', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvp0vz6wykf8gcb12r3hzf/barista---politis---santorini', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:48', 'AIRCANTEEN AE', 'Ζητείται Barista-Πωλητής σε κατάστημα εστίασης στο αεροδρόμιο της Σαντορίνης. Αν σου αρέσει η δυναμική ατμόσφαιρα του αεροδρομίου και έχεις πάθος για τον καφέ και την εξυπηρέτηση, σε περιμένουμε στην ομάδα μας! Η Air Canteen, εταιρία εστίασης που δραστηριοποιείται σε καταστήματα εντός αεροδρομίων και άλλων κλειστών αγορών, αναζητά άτομα με αγάπη για την εξυπηρέτηση, τα οποία θα προσφέρουν στους ταξιδιώτες μια αξέχαστη εμπειρία. Στη θέση αυτή, θα είσαι υπεύθυνος/η για την εξυπηρέτηση των πελατών μας με ευγένεια και επαγγελματισμό, φροντίζοντας να απολαμβάνουν την καλύτερη γευστική εμπειρία στο κατάστημά μας. Θα προετοιμάζεις ροφήματα υψηλής ποιότητας, ενώ ταυτόχρονα θα είσαι δίπλα στους πελάτες παρέχοντάς τους πληροφορίες και βοηθώντας τους να επιλέξουν τα προϊόντα που ταιριάζουν στις προτιμήσεις τους. Αρμοδιότητες: Προετοιμασία καφέ και άλλων ροφημάτων υψηλής ποιότητας Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών με χαμόγελο και προσοχή στη λεπτομέρεια Διατήρηση καθαριότητας και οργάνωσης στον χώρο εργασίας Συνεργασία με την ομάδα για τη δημιουργία μιας ευχάριστης εμπειρίας για κάθε πελάτη Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Εμπειρία ως barista ή σε παρόμοια θέση Ικανότητα επικοινωνίας και εξυπηρέτησης πελατών Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε βάρδιες Ικανότητα να εργάζεσαι υπό πίεση και να διαχειρίζεσαι πολλαπλά καθήκοντα Καλή γνώση αγγλικών Τι προσφέρουμε: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών Εκπαίδευση και υποστήριξη για την εξέλιξή σου Δυναμικό και φιλικό περιβάλλον εργασίας Πρόσβαση σε διεθνείς εμπειρίες με κάθε ταξιδιώτη Αν πιστεύεις ότι η θετική σου διάθεση και η αφοσίωσή σου στην εξυπηρέτηση μπορούν να κάνουν τη διαφορά, ανυπομονούμε να σε γνωρίσουμε! Στείλε το βιογραφικό σου σήμερα και γίνε μέλος της ομάδας μας σε έναν χώρο γεμάτο προορισμούς και ευκαιρίες!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
INSERT INTO `skywalker` (`id`, `title`, `url`, `location`, `posted`, `scraped`, `company`, `description`, `type`) VALUES
(784979, 'Senior Sommelier', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvpg1v8er7yb4n97yvgfxe/senior-sommelier', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:48', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Senior Sommelier to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Senior Sommelier supports the Head of Wines in delivering an exceptional wine experience, leading by example on the floor, mentoring Sommeliers, and ensuring operational excellence, cost control, and guest satisfaction. The Senior Sommelier reports to the Head of Wines. As Senior Sommelier, you will be responsible for the following duties: Support the Head of Wines in leading the sommelier function during service, ensuring consistent service excellence, strong team performance, and exceptional guest satisfaction. Assist the Head of Wines with administrative duties. Drive kind and generous service by role-modelling respectful, professional behavior towards both guests and colleagues, while maintaining daily communication with F&B and Culinary colleagues. Demonstrate outstanding food and wine knowledge, confidently recommending and pairing wines, supporting wine list execution, and enhancing the overall dining experience. Mentor Sommeliers, assist with the wine training and development of the F&B Service and Bar colleagues and support ongoing learning initiatives. Support operational controls including beverage charging accuracy, stock management, cellar organization, and preparation for monthly stock takes, while ensuring compliance with Mandarin Oriental standards and budgets. Attend required meetings and report maintenance issues. As Senior Sommelier, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit Sommelier certification is mandatory Experience in a similar role Fluency in English Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant Uniform and laundry of uniform Private Medical Insurance We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784980, 'Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvg6f07hd5h1fxsbz711gm/waiter', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:50', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Waiter to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Waiter provides the highest level of service and professional excellence, while being ever present in the outlet operation. The Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties: Provide respectful and generous service to both guests and colleagues. Follow all service steps thoroughly, requesting assistance promptly to avoid service delays. Manage the opening and closing of the outlet, including mise en place and setup. Maintain cleanliness in service and back-of-house areas. Attend pre-service briefings and ensure tasks are followed up efficiently. Operate the POS system and prepare bills accurately. As Waiter, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Experience in F&B service. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784981, 'Bartender - Κρήτη', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvhf0cje1j85hfwc67n396/bartender---kriti', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:50', 'AQUILA HOTELS & RESORTS', 'Η Aquila Hotels & Resorts, είναι ένας από τους πλέον καινοτόμους ξενοδοχειακούς ομίλους της Κρήτης – διαθέτοντας τέσσερις από τις πιο διάσημες μονάδες 5* του νησιού. Η φιλοξενία είναι για εμάς τρόπος ζωής και η πολυτέλεια, το πάθος μας. Η έμπειρη ομάδα καταρτισμένου ανθρώπινου δυναμικού με πολυετή εμπειρία στον κλάδο, είναι το στοιχείο που μας φέρνει στην κορυφή. Στόχος μας είναι να εμπλουτίσουμε την ομάδα του εκάστοτε ξενοδοχείου με νέους επαγγελματίες, που επιθυμούν να αναδειχθούν στον συναρπαστικό κόσμο του τουρισμού. Στείλε μας το βιογραφικό σου και κάνε την αίτησή σου τώρα για την θέση Bartender Απαιτούμενα προσόντα: Γνώση σερβιρίσματος οίνου, αποσταγμάτων και καφέ Εμπειρία σε αντίστοιχη ή παρεμφερή θέση Πολύ καλή γνώση της αγγλικής γλώσσας (επιθυμητή η γνώση της γερμανικής γλώσσας) Διαπροσωπικές και επικοινωνιακές ικανότητες Επαγγελματική συμπεριφορά Να διακατέχεται από συνέπεια και αποτελεσματικότητα Βασικές γνώσεις διαδικασιών υγιεινής, ασφάλειας και διαχείρισης τροφίμων και ποτών Εστίαση στην παροχή υπηρεσιών υψηλού επιπέδου Παροχές: Ευχάριστο περιβάλλον εργασίας Συνεχής επιμόρφωση στις νέες τάσεις της τουριστικής αγοράς Ελκυστικό πακέτο αποδοχών και προοπτικές επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης Δυνατότητα διαμονής Επισκεφτείτε την ιστοσελίδα μας: www.aquilahotels.com και στο πεδίο «Καριέρα» συμπληρώστε την ηλεκτρονική φόρμα επισυνάπτοντας το βιογραφικό σας.', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784982, 'F&B Host / Hostess', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvdzyt75jmvvqqtf38djjd/f-b-host---hostess', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:52', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an F&B Host/Hostess to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the F&B Host/Hostess is responsible to provide the highest level of service and professional excellence, being ever present in the operation, ensuring the highest standards and satisfying completely our guests during their meal experience. The F&B Host/Hostess reports to the F&B Supervisor. As F&B Host/Hostess, you will be responsible for the following duties: Support restaurant operations, including greeting, seating, and resetting tables. Provide kind and professional service to both guests and colleagues. Manage reservations using the SevenRooms system, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. Assist with guest inquiries, special requests, and communicate key information to the team. Maintain cleanliness, organisation, and stock of menus, newspapers, and surroundings. Respond proactively to guest feedback, ensuring satisfaction and effective communication. As F&B Host/Hostess, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Working experience in a similar role. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784983, 'In Room Dining Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvf3e8xqe4fmn0m28dygjj/in-room-dining-waiter', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:52', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an In Room Dining Waiter to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the In Room Dining Waiter is responsible to provide the highest level of service and professional excellence, being ever present in the operation, ensuring the highest standards and completely satisfying our guests during their meal experience. The In Room Dining Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As In Room Dining Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties: Ensure mise en place is prepared for efficient In Room Dining service. Have full knowledge of the menu, take orders professionally, and up-sell products. Handle billing, special requests, and guest complaints efficiently. Prioritize guest satisfaction, proactive communication, and workplace safety. Ensure cleanliness, order accuracy, and compliance with service standards. Maintain a professional appearance, uniform, and hygiene standards. As In Room Dining Waiter, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit Valid driving license Experience in F&B service. Experience in a similar role will be considered as a plus. Fluency in English Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784984, 'Pool Lifeguard', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvbyhzec38dq7bzpdrb0em/pool-lifeguard', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:54', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Pool Lifeguard to join our Security team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job: Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Security Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Pool Lifeguard ensures the safety of pool users by enforcing rules, maintaining cleanliness, conducting emergency checks, and responding to emergencies promptly while also reporting any safety hazards or defects. The Pool Lifeguard reports to the Lifeguard Supervisor. As Pool Lifeguard, you will be responsible for the following duties: Remain alert to emergency conditions and perform lifeguarding skills. Enforce rules and regulations and handle public enquires & feedback. Maintain works and cleaning to prevent defects and rust. Ensure the first-aid and lifesaving equipment are in good working condition. Conduct emergency phone checking on regular basis. Report potential safety and any defects of swimming pool facilities to the Engineering department. Ensure appropriate attire of the pool users and prevent hazard objects in the pool. As Pool Lifeguard, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Certified by ENKA or similar. BLS Certified. CPR Certified. First Aid Certificate. Experience in a similar position will be considered as a plus. Good level in English.  Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(784985, 'Assistant Store Manager #Sneaker10 - Ζάκυνθος', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmvdpeea4na0c6bv9mz2118/assistant-store-manager--sneaker10----zakynthos', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:54', 'COSMOS SPORT SA', 'Assistant Store Manager #Sneaker10 Ζάκυνθος #New Store Cosmos Sport SA, member of JD Sports Fashion Plc, founded in September of 1982. First store opened in Heraklion-Crete and since then the network expanded 98 further physical stores in Greece & Cyprus, 5 retail brands (JD Sports, Cosmos Sport, Sneaker10, Slamdunk, Rundome) 8 on-line shops and thousands of happy customers in Greece and Cyprus. Cosmos Sport is a constantly growing omnichannel company with a strong passion for sportswear, street style and limited items. Our team consists of 1800+ highly skilled, self-motivated young people, who love sports and have a passion for innovation! We are proud that Cosmossport.gr is now the No1 on-line store in the industry also selling abroad, having been awarded for 7 consecutive years as the best online sports shop in the country in e-volution Awards. We are excited being a preferred partner for global brands like Nike, Adidas, Reebok in the SEE. We are looking for a talented and passionate Assistant Store Manager for our Cosmos Sport store in Zakynthos! Job Overview: Assistant Store Managers are accountable for every aspect of the retail store operations, ensuring that all areas of the store are engaged, performing, and delivering world-class guest experience. Assistant Store Managers build team capabilities to drive strategy and achieve key results for the business. This role is responsible for the talent acquisition, ongoing people development and growth within their community. Responsibilities Customer Maintain an exceptional service experience in store, ensuring high level customers’ satisfaction. Foster a Client centric mindset by developing and maintaining solid Client relationships. Implement, in partnership with other company functions, clienteling initiatives and events and securing Client loyalty. Team Train, mentor, motivate and offer constructive feedback to the team. Support team members (e.g., leading by example or coaching) to ensure a great guest experience. Promote an entrepreneurial and team spirit approach, using effective communication, ensuring efficient organization and professional growth. Ensure a hazard-free, safe and healthy working environment in compliance with regulations. Ensure the team is always informed about product, policies and procedures. Attract and recruit the best talents available on the market through networking and scouting. Retail Lead and manage all the day-to-day operational activities of the store and ensure compliance with policies and procedures. Monitor and control store productivity levels with an aim to achieve targeted KPIs. Implement personnel and resource planning strategies to optimize staff schedules. Work extensively in partnership with the Marketing, VM, Commercial dept. in order to build strong customer retention. Requirements University Degree or equivalent qualification A minimum of 2 years’ experience of managing a standalone retail store (or Department Store floor) Excellent use of English language and computer skills Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal skills Numerical and analytical knowledge to monitor KPIs Sound working knowledge of Microsoft Office Leadership skills and business orientation Excellent communicator, with a positive, open and progressive, energetic, motivating, personal style Customer service orientation with in-depth knowledge of basic business management processes Passion for sports and fashion Willingness to learn and tackle new challenges Benefits Competitive compensation package & performance bonus Career development opportunities & education programs Health & wellness programs to keep you active One day off, part of our \"parents’ day off\" program Free Diagnostic Tests for all our employees at the Euromedica Group\'s diagnostic centres Generous employee discount in all our brands (JD Sports,Cosmos Sport, Sneaker10, Slamdunk, Rundome) Up to 75% discount at the European University of Cyprus (face-to-face or online attendance) Extras, discounts and perks - Being a valued member of Cosmos Sport team means a lot to us! We offer a variety of 100+ cool extras! Link here At Cosmos Sport, we are committed to providing a great place to work for all of our people, without regard tο race, religion, color, sex, national origin, age, sexual orientations, genders, or disability.  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(784986, 'Πωλητής/ρια Καταστήματος', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kpmtxv5ddrrtk3f708e159g3/politis-ria-katastimatos', 'n/a', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-20 08:00:56', 'ΘΑΛΑΜΙ', 'Ζητείται πωλήτρια για εργασία σε τουριστικό κατάστημα. Αρμοδιότητες: Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών με ευγένεια και επαγγελματισμό Προώθηση και πώληση προϊόντων Διατήρηση καθαριότητας και τάξης στον χώρο εργασίας Διαχείριση ταμείου Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Καλή γνώση Αγγλικών (επιπλέον γλώσσες θα εκτιμηθούν) Επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητες και ομαδικό πνεύμα Προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση επιθυμητή αλλά όχι απαραίτητη Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Παροχές: Ανταγωνιστικός μισθός Παροχή διαμονής Ευχάριστο και υποστηρικτικό εργασιακό περιβάλλον Πλήρης ασφάλιση', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
