riendly and kind personality, with team spirit Degree in Hospitality / Tourism (desirable) We offer: Accommodation and meals Competitive remuneration package Continuous training (Departmental and Generic) Excellent working environment Development opportunities within a fast-growing group of luxury 5-star properties Should you wish to join the Myconian Collection team, please forward us your CV with a recent photo. All applications will be considered confidential.  ', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796046, 'Πωλητής/ρια Καταστήματος - Χαλάνδρι', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy6kqzrcmkk279q3yx22art/politis-ria-katastimatos', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:32', 'PASSARELLA A.E.', 'Τα ζαχαροπλαστεία Passarella αναζητούν Πωλήτριες - Πωλητές για το κατάστημα στο Χαλάνδρι Παρέχονται: Πενθήμερη εργασία Πλήρης ασφαλιστική κάλυψη 14 μισθοί ετησίως Εκπτωτική κάρτα  Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Υπευθυνότητα Προθυμία Συνεργασία Συνέπεια Επαγγελματισμός Αρμοδιότητες: Παραλαβή και τακτοποίηση προϊόντων Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών και επίλυση σχετικών ερωτημάτων Ημερήσιες και μηνιαίες απογραφές προϊόντων Παραγγελιοληψία προϊόντων  Τήρηση αρχείων υγειονομικού χαρακτήρα Ημερήσιες, εβδομαδιαίες και μηνιαίες καθαριότητες Ταμειακές συναλλαγές', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796047, 'Πωλήτριες / Πωλητές - Μαρούσι', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy6m93394k4fmr7fyg0462v/politries---polites---marousi', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:33', 'PASSARELLA A.E.', 'Τα ζαχαροπλαστεία Passarella αναζητούν Πωλήτριες - Πωλητές για το νέο μας κατάστημα στο Μαρούσι  Παρέχονται: Πενθήμερη εργασία, Πλήρης ασφαλιστική κάλυψη, 14 μισθοί ετησίως, Εκπτωτική κάρτα  Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Υπευθυνότητα Προθυμία Συνεργασία Συνέπεια Επαγγελματισμός Αρμοδιότητες: Παραλαβή και τακτοποίηση προϊόντων Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών και επίλυση σχετικών ερωτημάτων Ημερήσιες και μηνιαίες απογραφές προϊόντων Παραγγελιοληψία προϊόντων  Τήρηση αρχείων υγειονομικού χαρακτήρα Ημερήσιες, εβδομαδιαίες και μηνιαίες καθαριότητες Ταμειακές συναλλαγές', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796048, 'Οδηγός', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy5vbabq09skwpcc7ym4jtz/odigos', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:34', 'SPIRIT SUPPLIES', 'Εταιρεία που δραστηριοποιείται στο εμπόριο τροφίμων και στην τροφοδοσία τελικών σημείων αναζητά: Οδηγό Απαραίτητα προσόντα οδηγού: Δίπλωμα οδήγησης Β\' ή Γ\' κατηγορίας επιθυμητό Γνώση του λεκανοπεδίου Αττικής Εκπληρωμένες στρατιωτικές υποχρεώσεις Επαγγελματική εμφάνιση και συμπεριφορά Συνέπεια και υπευθυνότητα Προϋπηρεσία σε ανάλογη θέση Κύρια καθήκοντα οδηγού: Παράδοση των εμπορευμάτων στους πελάτες της εταιρίας Μέριμνα για την ορθή χρήση των οχημάτων Ευθύνη για τη συντήρηση και την επισκευή των οχημάτων Τήρηση κανόνων υγιεινής και ασφάλειας Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών σύμφωνα με την εμπειρία και τις ικανότητες του υποψηφίου Πρόσθετη ιδιωτική ασφαλιστική κάλυψη  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796049, 'Υπάλληλος Γραφείου', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kbqrqhmtzwz91kcbk1dx6ksc/ypallilos-grafeiou', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:34', 'EFTERPIS PARKING', 'Υπόγειος χώρος στάθμευσης οχημάτων στο Μαρούσι αναζητά Υπάλληλο Γραφείου για μόνιμη, πλήρους απασχόλησης συνεργασία. Πρόκειται για οργανωμένο, σύγχρονο και ευχάριστο εργασιακό περιβάλλον με 24ωρη λειτουργία. Πενθήμερη εργασία - 8ωρή - σε κυλιόμενες βάρδιες (Πρωινή-απογευματινή-βραδινή). Καθήκοντα θέσης:  Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών & διαχείριση ταμείου  Παρακολούθηση και επίβλεψη της ομαλής λειτουργίας της βάρδιας  Βασικές εργασίες γραφείου  Συντονισμός με την ομάδα για καθημερινές ανάγκες του χώρου Απαραίτητα προσόντα:  Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια  Ευγένεια και καλή συμπεριφορά  Όρεξη για δουλειά και διάθεση συνεργασίας  Βασική γνώση χειρισμού Η/Υ Παροχές:  Ικανοποιητικός μισθός  Πενθήμερη εργασία - 8ωρη - σε κυλιόμενες βάρδιες (Πρωινή-απογευματινή-βραδινή)  Σταθερή σχέση εργασίας αορίστου χρόνου  Όλα τα νόμιμα (δώρα, άδειες κ.λπ.)  Φιλικό εργασιακό περιβάλλον Επικοινωνία και αποστολή υποψήφιων βιογραφικών αποκλειστικά μόνο μέσω της πλατφόρμας.', 'Σύμβαση αορίστου χρόνου'),
(796050, 'Προσωπικό Πώλησης για το τμήμα του Κρεοπωλείου- Κέντρο Αθηνών', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy4rf4fcxb443pmchty1kez/prosopiko-polisis-gia-to-tmima-tou-kreopoleiou--kentro-athinon', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:36', 'ΑΝΕΔΗΚ ΚΡΗΤΙΚΟΣ Α.Ε.', 'Η αλυσίδα ΑΝΕΔΗΚ ΚΡΗΤΙΚΟΣ Α.Ε, με παρουσία σε όλη την Ελλάδα, επιθυμεί να προσλάβει για τα καταστήματά της στο Κέντρο Αθηνών: Προσωπικό Πώλησης για το τμήμα του Κρεοπωλείου Βασικές αρμοδιότητες: Μεριμνάτε για την άρτια εξυπηρέτηση των πελατών σύμφωνα με τις ανάγκες τους Φροντίζετε για τη σωστή σήμανση και ποικιλία της «βιτρίνας» σας Εφαρμόζετε τους κανονισμούς υγιεινής και πολιτικής της εταιρίας Προφίλ υποψηφίου: Έχετε Επικοινωνιακές ικανότητες Έχετε ευχάριστη προσωπικότητα και αποτελείτε πρότυπο ευγένειας απέναντι στους πελάτες Σας διακρίνουν υπευθυνότητα και αξιοπιστία Σας αρέσει η ομαδική εργασία και οι κοινοί στόχοι Εκπληρωμένες στρατιωτικές υποχρεώσεις για τους άνδρες υποψηφίους Η εταιρεία προσφέρει: Εργάζεστε σε ένα σύγχρονο και οργανωμένο περιβάλλον αναλαμβάνοντας μία ποικιλόμορφη εργασία Μέσα από ένα πρόγραμμα εκπαίδευσης σας παρέχουμε τα απαραίτητα εφόδια για τη θέση σας, ώστε να ενσωματωθείτε στη φιλοσοφία της εταιρίας μας Δυνατότητα επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης και ανάπτυξης Για όλα τα βιογραφικά θα τηρηθεί απόλυτη εχεμύθεια. Θα απαντηθούν μόνο οι υποψηφιότητες που πληρούν τις προϋποθέσεις.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796051, 'Αποθηκάριος', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy5sntf65d0n8a4k8mswkbc/apothikarios', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:38', 'SPIRIT SUPPLIES', 'Εταιρεία που δραστηριοποιείται στο εμπόριο τροφίμων και στην τροφοδοσία τελικών σημείων αναζητά:  Αποθηκάριο  Κύρια καθήκοντα : Παραλαβή, έλεγχος και τακτοποίηση προϊόντων  στην αποθήκη Προετοιμασία παραγγελιών για διανομή ( picking/ packing ) Έλεγχος αποθεμάτων και ενημέρωση συστημάτων/υπευθύνων Τήρηση κανόνων υγιεινής και ασφαλούς αποθήκευσης τροφίμων Συνεργασία με οδηγούς και τμήμα πωλήσεων για ομαλή ροή εργασιών Απαραίτητα προσόντα : Προϋπηρεσία σε ανάλογη θέση Συνέπεια και υπευθυνότητα Οργανωτικές δεξιότητες Εκπληρωμένες στρατιωτικές υποχρεώσεις Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών σύμφωνα με την εμπειρία, τις ικανότητες του υποψηφίου Πρόσθετη ιδιωτική ασφαλιστική κάλυψη Σταθερό ωράριο απασχόλησης Δυνατότητες εξέλιξης, αρμοδιοτήτων και αποδοχών      ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796055, 'Driver D’ - Santorini', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqy3ccz9v8msqxjdrxzfkn59/driver-d%E2%80%99---santorini', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:01:40', 'Andronis', 'ANDRONIS is currently recruiting Driver D’ (based in Santoriri) We are looking for a Driver D’ who wants to move his/her career forward. If this sounds as a great challenge, why don ‘t you join Andronis team consisting of 5 hotels in Santorini and Paros, with more than 600 employees, all driven by an inspiring purpose of providing the finest services around the world  About us Memories that matter, from people who care We are passionate about creating unforgettable moments and memories. We achieve this by ensuring that our guests truly enjoy simple pleasures. Each Andronis hotel is inspired by the landscape in which it is located, respecting the cultural heritage of the area. Our team is devoted to offering the warmest hospitality and unparalleled service to all our guests. Cosmopolitan life at its best & authenticity is what lies at the heart of the #AndronisExperience. Meet the team Our team consists of people with vision and passion for what they do. Our employees are our greatest asset and our greatest investment. We are committed to offering continuous training, personal development and support for each team member. On a daily basis, the management of the company, as well as a team of Mental Health scientists, take care of the well-being of every employee and each team on a personal and professional level.  As a Driver D’ you will Conduct on-the-job training in accordance with departmental standards and procedures Inspect company vehicles Report maintenance needs and vehicle malfunctions Comply with the traffic code and driving regulations Contribute to maintaining high standards of cleanliness and safety Qualifications Previous work experience Fluency in Greek, both spoken and written, is required Knowledge of English is desirable Valid Class D professional driver’s license Professional appearance and behavior, with a focus on delivering high-quality service Excellent communication skills Team spirit and ability to collaborate effectively with all departments Responsibility and organizational skills We offer: Accommodation with air conditioning, Wi-Fi, access to laundry facilities, and access to our outdoor gym Opportunities for continuous training Employee Assistance Program (support line for employees and their family members for personal and professional matters) Provision of work uniforms Discounted prices at the employee Mini Market Two meals per day at the staff restaurant Transportation to and from work• Discounted prices at selected Andronis Restaurants Why Be Part of Our Journey? It is a unique chance for you to work in one of the fastest growing hotel groups in Greece, alongside dedicated colleagues and professionals. Being a part of Andronis is not “just a job”. There is purpose, passion, and meaning in what we do. We place great emphasis on passion and team spirit – reasons why our well-rehearsed team has been together for many years. The goal Andronis set from the beginning is the provision of high-standard services for its customers, partners and the society of Santorini and Paros. A valuable pillar for Andronis is its staff, who are considered the most essential image of the company. Our Promise to You: Andronis offers an energizing workplace adopting an open culture and transparent communication. We encourage a collaborative working environment while offering development opportunities for our employees. All our employees are treated with respect, while we strive to ensure you have the tools and resources you need to be successful. Andronis is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, age, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, pregnancy, color, citizenship or any other group protected by the law.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796088, 'Retail Store Assistant Manager / Sales Associate', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqw19xqt0tsg68rkmma5vm7y/retail-store-assistant-manager---sales-associate', 'n/a', '2026-05-05', '2026-05-06 16:02:14', 'Workathlon', 'Retail Store Assistant Manager / Sales Associate – Anthologist Boutique Location: Athens, Greece About Us: Anthologist stores, located in the city of Athens within Conrad Athens The Ilisian, are seeking to recruit an Assistant Manager / Sales Associate. With international recognition from leading media such as Vogue, Conde Nast Traveler, and Monocle, Anthologist’s retail presence extends across carefully curated environments that blend design, culture, and hospitality. Based in Athens, Anthologist is a cross-cultural brand rooted in retail, hospitality, and design, led by Greek-American Andria Mitsakos. Championing cultural preservation as a living practice, it creates objects, sculpts fashion, imagines spaces, and tells stories that bridge tradition with contemporary expression. Through global collaborations, Anthologist shapes meaningful environments where retail becomes an immersive, storytelling-driven experience. Role Overview: The Retail Store Assistant Manager / Sales Associate plays a dual role, combining elevated client service with operational and team support responsibilities. This position is instrumental in ensuring the seamless day-to-day running of the boutique, while delivering a high-touch, experiential retail journey aligned with Anthologist’s philosophy. Key Responsibilities: Deliver exceptional, personalized customer service, elevating the in-store experience through storytelling and product knowledge Act as a brand ambassador, representing Anthologist both within the store and in external interactions Support the Store Manager in overseeing daily operations, including opening/closing procedures and workflow coordination Assist in guiding, motivating, and supporting team members to achieve sales targets and service excellence Handle customer inquiries, feedback, and complaints with professionalism and a solution-oriented mindset Build, manage, and maintain a strong customer database, fostering long-term client relationships Contribute to the planning and execution of in-store and local events Ensure visual merchandising standards and overall store presentation align with brand and hotel guidelines Monitor stock levels, oversee inventory processes, and ensure proper product rotation and availability Analyze store performance and contribute insights and action plans to improve results Review sales reports and suggest merchandising or operational improvements Create and support content for social media, reflecting the brand’s aesthetic and storytelling approach Ensure full compliance with store SOPs and alignment with hotel policies Requirements: 2–4 years of experience in retail; experience in luxury retail or hospitality is highly desirable Previous exposure to supervisory or team support responsibilities is a strong plus Strong understanding of high-end customer service and experiential retail Analytical thinking with good command of MS Office and social media platforms Fluent in English; Greek or additional languages will be considered an asset Own transportation (car or equivalent) is required Candidate Profile: Highly organized with strong attention to detail and the ability to multitask effectively Proactive, confident, and solution-driven with a hands-on approach Strong aesthetic sensibility and appreciation for design, culture, and luxury retail Natural team player with emerging leadership skills Excellent communication and interpersonal abilities, comfortable with an international clientele Calm and effective problem-solver, capable of handling challenges with professionalism Benefits: Competitive remuneration package with performance-based incentives Opportunity to grow within an internationally recognized design-led brand Continuous training and development opportunities Inspiring, creative, and collaborative work environment Exposure to a unique intersection of retail, hospitality, and design', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796102, 'Barista', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqxvm3t76h795jd8mgbenh6z/barista', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:02:28', 'Mikel Coffee Company', 'Η Mikel Coffee Company, με δίκτυο καταστημάτων στην Ελλάδα όσο και στο εξωτερικό, με ηγετική θέση στην ελληνική αγορά της καφεστίασης, αναζητά άτομα με ζήλο και υπευθυνότητα για να συμπεριληφθούν στο δυναμικό της εταιρίας για την θέση: Barista για το κατάστημά μας στο Αιγάλεω. Προφίλ ιδανικού υποψηφίου: Ευχάριστη προσωπικότητα Μεθοδικότητα, ευχέρεια επικοινωνίας και ομαδικό πνεύμα εργασίας Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Η προϋπηρεσία στον χώρο της μαζικής εστίασης θα εκτιμηθεί Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Σύγχρονη και συνεχή εκπαίδευση Ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης εντός του οργανισμού Ευχάριστο και νεανικό περιβάλλον Πλήρες πακέτο αποδοχών Πλήρη απασχόληση σε κυλιόμενο ωράριο Για όλες τις αιτήσεις θα τηρηθεί απόλυτη εχεμύθεια.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796103, 'Barista - Αγ. Ιωάννης Ρέντης', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqxvz340ch1zch9rm9815ram/barista---ag--ioannis-rentis', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:02:28', 'Mikel Coffee Company', 'Η Mikel Coffee Company, με δίκτυο καταστημάτων στην Ελλάδα όσο και στο εξωτερικό, με ηγετική θέση στην ελληνική αγορά της καφεστίασης, αναζητά άτομα με ζήλο και υπευθυνότητα για να συμπεριληφθούν στο δυναμικό της εταιρίας για την θέση: Barista για το κατάστημά μας στον Άγιο Ιωάννη Ρέντη Προφίλ ιδανικού υποψηφίου: Ευχάριστη προσωπικότητα Μεθοδικότητα, ευχέρεια επικοινωνίας και ομαδικό πνεύμα εργασίας Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Η προϋπηρεσία στον χώρο της μαζικής εστίασης θα εκτιμηθεί Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Σύγχρονη και συνεχή εκπαίδευση Ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης εντός του οργανισμού Ευχάριστο και νεανικό περιβάλλον Πλήρες πακέτο αποδοχών Πλήρη απασχόληση σε κυλιόμενο ωράριο Για όλες τις αιτήσεις θα τηρηθεί απόλυτη εχεμύθεια.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796105, 'Barista - Εμπορικό Πάρκο Αεροδρομίου', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqxvbabpbcy98gkh2hw1ndfq/barista---emporiko-parko-aerodromiou', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 16:02:30', 'Mikel Coffee Company', 'Η Mikel Coffee Company, με δίκτυο καταστημάτων στην Ελλάδα όσο και στο εξωτερικό, με ηγετική θέση στην ελληνική αγορά της καφεστίασης, αναζητά άτομα με ζήλο και υπευθυνότητα για να συμπεριληφθούν στο δυναμικό της εταιρίας για τη θέση Barista Προφίλ ιδανικού υποψηφίου: Ευχάριστη προσωπικότητα Μεθοδικότητα, ευχέρεια επικοινωνίας και ομαδικό πνεύμα εργασίας Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Η προϋπηρεσία στον χώρο της μαζικής εστίασης θα εκτιμηθεί Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Σύγχρονη και συνεχή εκπαίδευση Ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης εντός του οργανισμού Ευχάριστο και νεανικό περιβάλλον Πλήρες πακέτο αποδοχών ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796120, 'Προϊστάμενος/η Λογιστηρίου (Chief Accountant / Accounting Manager)', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqw12fhhqncrvvtvwvba5vvt/proistamenos-i-logistiriou--chief-accountant---accounting-manager-', 'n/a', '2026-05-05', '2026-05-06 16:02:49', 'Δυναμικά αναπτυσσόμενη Εταιρεία', 'Περιγραφή Εταιρείας Δυναμικά αναπτυσσόμενη εταιρεία με ηγετική παρουσία στον τομέα των συστημάτων ηλεκτρονικής ασφάλειας και των βιομηχανικών αυτοματισμών, αναζητά: Προϊστάμενος/η Λογιστηρίου (Chief Accountant / Accounting Manager)  Περιγραφή ρόλου Ο/Η κατάλληλος/η υποψήφιος/α θα αναφέρεται απευθείας στον Διευθύνοντα Σύμβουλο και θα είναι υπεύθυνος/η για την εύρυθμη λειτουργία του λογιστηρίου και την υποστήριξη της διοίκησης σε θέματα οικονομικής διαχείρισης και αναφορών. Καθήκοντα: Οργάνωση, επίβλεψη και διαχείριση των καθημερινών εργασιών του Λογιστηρίου Συντονισμός και καθοδήγηση της ομάδας λογιστηρίου Σύνταξη και έλεγχος φορολογικών δηλώσεων (ΦΠΑ, ΦΜΥ, φόρος εισοδήματος) Σύνταξη οικονομικών καταστάσεων και ισολογισμού Ανάλυση οικονομικών στοιχείων και reporting προς τη διοίκηση Παρακολούθηση ταμειακών ροών (cash flow) και budgeting Συνεργασία με εξωτερικούς ελεγκτές και φοροτεχνικούς Έλεγχος αποθεμάτων και διαδικασιών αποθήκης Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Πτυχίο ΑΕΙ οικονομικής ή λογιστικής κατεύθυνσης Προϋπηρεσία τουλάχιστον 15–20 ετών σε οργανωμένο λογιστήριο Εμπειρία σε θέση ευθύνης (Chief Accountant / Accounting Manager) Πολύ καλή γνώση Ελληνικών Λογιστικών Προτύπων (ΕΛΠ) και IFRS Άριστη γνώση της πλατφόρμας myDATA Πολύ καλή γνώση ERP συστημάτων (SoftOne θα θεωρηθεί ισχυρό πλεονέκτημα) Πολύ καλή γνώση Αγγλικών Ικανότητες οργάνωσης, διοίκησης ομάδας και αναλυτικής σκέψης Παροχές: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών (ανάλογα προσόντων) Σταθερό και δυναμικό περιβάλλον εργασίας Άμεση συνεργασία με τη διοίκηση της εταιρείας Προοπτικές εξέλιξης', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796149, 'Barista', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqvz0qbab7n7vethd0fke46m/barista', 'n/a', '2026-05-05', '2026-05-06 16:03:17', 'Ανώνυμη Εταιρία', 'Ζητείται Barista για εργασία σε πολυτελές 5άστερο ξενοδοχείο στο κέντρο της Αθήνας. Αρμοδιότητες: Παρασκευή και σερβίρισμα καφέ και ροφημάτων υψηλής ποιότητας Εξυπηρέτηση πελατών με επαγγελματισμό και ευγένεια Διατήρηση καθαριότητας και οργάνωσης του χώρου εργασίας Διαχείριση παραγγελιών και συνεργασία με την υπόλοιπη ομάδα Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση (ιδανικά σε ξενοδοχειακό περιβάλλον) Γνώση παρασκευής καφέ (espresso, cappuccino, latte art κ.λπ.) Πολύ καλή γνώση αγγλικών (επιπλέον γλώσσες θα εκτιμηθούν) Επαγγελματική εμφάνιση και επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητες Ομαδικό πνεύμα και συνέπεια Παροχές: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών Άριστο και σύγχρονο περιβάλλον εργασίας Δυνατότητες εξέλιξης σε έναν δυναμικό ξενοδοχειακό όμιλο Αν ενδιαφέρεστε να γίνετε μέλος μιας ομάδας υψηλών προδιαγραφών φιλοξενίας, αποστείλετε το βιογραφικό σας σημείωμα.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
INSERT INTO `skywalker` (`id`, `title`, `url`, `location`, `posted`, `scraped`, `company`, `description`, `type`) VALUES
(796217, 'Lifeguard - Skiathos', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kqz0jnvns967mxf8rq12etav/lifeguard---skiathos', 'n/a', '2026-05-06', '2026-05-06 22:00:36', 'KASSANDRA BAY', 'KB Collection Hotels & Resorts in Skiathos wishes to hire for season 2026: Lifeguard Responsibilities Set up umbrellas, loungers, and other pool furniture. Ensure that the pool furniture and area are clean and safe. Warn of unsafe activities and enforce water safety policies and pool regulations. Provide first aid in the event of injury, rescue swimmers in danger or distress and administer Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) or artificial respiration, if necessary. Assess conditions for safety and come up with an action plan for aquatics emergency. Inspect pool equipment, facilities and water to make sure they are usable and safe. Open and close the pool each day, depending on schedule and hours. Identify potential threats to safety and watches over guests to ensure they are safe. Contact appropriate persons in case a situation escalates beyond their expertise. Enforce the facility’s rules. Maintain a level of physical competence to carry out the job. Inspect facility and immediately report any unsafe conditions or equipment to supervisor. Requirements Lifeguard degree Certification in First aid, CPR, and AED principles and procedures Knowledge of water rescue methods and techniques, swimming strokes and aquatic techniques.= Physically fit Competent swimmer  At least 1 year working experience in a similar position, preferably in a 4* or 5* hotel Good knowledge and use of Greek and English both written and verbal (A second foreign language will be considered an asset.) Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to interact effectively with guests and team members Customer-focused attitude with an approachable and friendly demeanor Strong organizational and multitasking skills, with the ability to perform well in a fast-paced environment. Professional appearance and demeanor, including a neat and well-groomed appearance and the ability to maintain confidentiality We offer Accommodation Meal plan Professional, dynamic and pleasant working environment All required insurance Competitive salary package Chances for further development The company will contact only applicants whose qualifications meet the requirements for the requested position. Application details will remain confidential.', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796417, 'Pool Lifeguard', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0q4edmgj4b8aapkqdt75dh/pool-lifeguard', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:10', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Pool Lifeguard to join our Security team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Security Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Pool Lifeguard ensures the safety of pool users by enforcing rules, maintaining cleanliness, conducting emergency checks, and responding to emergencies promptly while also reporting any safety hazards or defects. The Pool Lifeguard reports to the Lifeguard Supervisor. As Pool Lifeguard, you will be responsible for the following duties: Remain alert to emergency conditions and perform lifeguarding skills. Enforce rules and regulations and handle public enquires & feedback. Maintain works and cleaning to prevent defects and rust. Ensure the first-aid and lifesaving equipment are in good working condition. Conduct emergency phone checking on regular basis. Report potential safety and any defects of swimming pool facilities to the Engineering department. Ensure appropriate attire of the pool users and prevent hazard objects in the pool. As Pool Lifeguard, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Certified by ENKA or similar. BLS Certified. CPR Certified. First Aid Certificate. Experience in a similar position will be considered as a plus. Good level in English.  Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796418, 'Senior Sommelier', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0ppn2t6m0yhm3sxcvmntma/senior-sommelier', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:11', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Senior Sommelier to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Senior Sommelier supports the Head of Wines in delivering an exceptional wine experience, leading by example on the floor, mentoring Sommeliers, and ensuring operational excellence, cost control, and guest satisfaction. The Senior Sommelier reports to the Head of Wines. As Senior Sommelier, you will be responsible for the following duties Support the Head of Wines in leading the sommelier function during service, ensuring consistent service excellence, strong team performance, and exceptional guest satisfaction. Assist the Head of Wines with administrative duties. Drive kind and generous service by role-modelling respectful, professional behavior towards both guests and colleagues, while maintaining daily communication with F&B and Culinary colleagues. Demonstrate outstanding food and wine knowledge, confidently recommending and pairing wines, supporting wine list execution, and enhancing the overall dining experience. Mentor Sommeliers, assist with the wine training and development of the F&B Service and Bar colleagues and support ongoing learning initiatives. Support operational controls including beverage charging accuracy, stock management, cellar organization, and preparation for monthly stock takes, while ensuring compliance with Mandarin Oriental standards and budgets. Attend required meetings and report maintenance issues. As Senior Sommelier, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit Sommelier certification is mandatory Experience in a similar role Fluency in English Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant Uniform and laundry of uniform Private Medical Insurance We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796419, 'In Room Dining Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0q2h6ma8d73fr58hy7fqt3/in-room-dining-waiter', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:14', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an In Room Dining Waiter to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the In Room Dining Waiter is responsible to provide the highest level of service and professional excellence, being ever present in the operation, ensuring the highest standards and completely satisfying our guests during their meal experience. The In Room Dining Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As In Room Dining Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties: Ensure mise en place is prepared for efficient In Room Dining service. Have full knowledge of the menu, take orders professionally, and up-sell products. Handle billing, special requests, and guest complaints efficiently. Prioritize guest satisfaction, proactive communication, and workplace safety. Ensure cleanliness, order accuracy, and compliance with service standards. Maintain a professional appearance, uniform, and hygiene standards. As In Room Dining Waiter, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit Valid driving license Experience in F&B service. Experience in a similar role will be considered as a plus. Fluency in English Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796420, 'F&B Supervisor', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0pmzvqpghbmr0d7mvav3sh/f-b-supervisor', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:14', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an F&B Supervisor to join our Food & Beverage Team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the F&B Supervisor provides efficient and friendly service, ensuring guests and residents satisfaction is achieved throughout their experience, whilst also providing the team with support. The F&B Supervisor reports to the Assistant Restaurant Manager. As F&B Supervisor, you will be responsible for the following duties Oversee and manage shifts effectively to ensure a smooth and effective overall operation, by guiding colleagues on and by personally involving himself/herself in all aspects of the sequence of service. Provide direction and support to all outlet colleagues at any time, particularly during the operational hours. Support the management team when required to train colleagues, in accordance with the applicable standards and policies. Follow the side duty schedule and assure all tasks are completed at all times in a timely manner. Assure the back and front of house areas of the outlet are clean and tidy at all times. Identify areas for improvement in F&B service and quality, through guest comments, comment cards and guest incident reports, and share observations and recommendations with the management team. As F&B Supervisor, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit 2 years\' experience in a similar role, in a luxury hotel operation Fluency in English Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant Uniform and laundry of uniform Private Medical Insurance We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796421, 'Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0pnh87tvy6tr2z77gnz71j/waiter', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:16', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a  Waiter  to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Waiter provides the highest level of service and professional excellence, while being ever present in the outlet operation. The Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties Provide respectful and generous service to both guests and colleagues. Follow all service steps thoroughly, requesting assistance promptly to avoid service delays. Manage the opening and closing of the outlet, including mise en place and setup. Maintain cleanliness in service and back-of-house areas. Attend pre-service briefings and ensure tasks are followed up efficiently. Operate the POS system and prepare bills accurately. As Waiter, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Experience in F&B service. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796422, 'Junior Sous Chef', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0pfhzsrdz9hbqwdwt7g2m5/junior-sous-chef', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:17', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Junior Sous Chef to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Junior Sous Chef ensures the smooth running of culinary operations and the good working environment between colleagues. The Junior Sous Chef reports to the Sous Chef.  As Junior Sous Chef, you will be responsible for the following duties Check the quality of all food production in the kitchen, ensure all live products received are in top condition and are of top quality, oversee stock rotation (F.I.F.O.) and carry out the kitchen requisitioning and ordering. Check standard recipes ensuring proper portion control and uniformity of taste and quality. Oversee the overall food cost, as well as kitchen supplies, kitchen energy costs and kitchen utensils. Propose, and initiate when approved, new services and products for our guests. Motivate and lead by example. Ensure that all designated action points from daily briefings or other operational meetings are being followed by the individuals concerned. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Junior Sous Chef, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 1-2 years of experience in a similar role. Good level in English.  Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
