(796427, 'Commis (Γ\' Μάγειρας)', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0p7y56aa0aqfbwqbmp5z8w/commis--g--mageiras-', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:20', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Commis to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Commis carries out kitchen duties whilst ensuring smooth, coordinated team effort in the kitchen. The Commis reports to the Junior Sous Chef. As Commis, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Work closely with the Culinary team on daily operations and food quality control. Ensure proper food handling, monitor raw food availability, and inspect incoming goods. Attend all training sessions and participate in special events, promotions, and demonstrations. Maintain a clean, presentable uniform and ensure personal hygiene. Inform the Executive Chef and Chef de Cuisine regarding operational issues. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Commis, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. 1 year of culinary experience. Good level in English or Greek.  Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Με φυσική παρουσία'),
(796428, 'Steward (Λαντζιέρης / Λαντζιέρισσα)', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0p4peb6z9hs5k2jezq0mhj/steward--lantzieris---lantzierissa-', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:22', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for Stewards to join our Culinary team, for season 2026.  Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Steward assists in keeping the kitchen clean, in sanitizing and in keeping the workflows of dirt and dishes and equipment clean. The Steward reports to the Stewarding Supervisor. As Steward, you will be responsible for the following duties Clean and sanitize work surfaces, equipment, dishes, and utensils. Maintain cleanliness standards by washing dishes, pots, pans, plates, silverware, glassware, and other items used in cooking or food preparation. Operate dishwashers and other equipment used for cleaning and sterilizing dishes, glassware, utensils, pots, pans, and other kitchen items. Clean and maintain the kitchen, including sweeping floors and wiping down surfaces. Follow safety procedures for using equipment, disposing of waste products, and other activities. Support the Culinary team. As Steward, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Experience in a similar role will be considered as a plus. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία');
INSERT INTO `skywalker` (`id`, `title`, `url`, `location`, `posted`, `scraped`, `company`, `description`, `type`) VALUES
(796429, 'Spa Therapist', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0p932406w5wqdjc0m7rkp0/spa-therapist', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:22', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Spa Therapist to join our Spa & Wellness team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Spa & Wellness Department in Pylos, the Spa Therapist is responsible for enlightening the guests on various body treatments, massage techniques, and spa services and for customising the massage treatments as per the guest’s requirements. The Spa Therapist reports to the Head Therapist. As Spa Therapist, you will be responsible for the following duties Deliver spa treatments while ensuring guest comfort and satisfaction. Maintain cleanliness, organisation, and high service standards in the spa in line with Mandarin Oriental procedures. Attend meetings and trainings to maintain professional standards. Recommend and upsell spa products and services to enhance guest experience. Report equipment issues and ensure inventory is well-stocked. Assist in various spa operations, including front desk, retail, and relaxation areas. As Spa Therapist, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. License in Physiotherapy or related field is mandatory. Good level in English. Experience as a licensed spa therapist in a luxury hotel. Working knowledge of skin care therapies, beauty products and trends will be considered as a plus. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796430, 'Stewarding Supervisor', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0p52qkbse3314a0y2hkdpk/stewarding-supervisor', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:24', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Stewarding Supervisor to join our Stewarding team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Stewarding Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Stewarding Supervisor oversees the work of the Stewards, ensuring that all areas are kept clean and free of hazards. The Stewarding Supervisor reports to the Back of House Manager. As Stewarding Supervisor, you will be responsible for the following duties Maintain the cleanliness of all stewarding areas and kitchen equipment, while keeping accurate records of cleaning schedules and chemicals used.  Lead, train and supervise the Stewarding Team, while ensuring Mandarin Oriental standards are followed. Ensure all set-ups and supplies are in place for each function. Ensure all breakages and chipped items are removed from circulation and inventoried for warranty. Ensure all kitchen equipment is in working order, report any items in need of repair and create an engineering request. Maintain a clean and safe work environment for all colleagues. As Stewarding Supervisor, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Previous working experience as a Stewarding Supervisor or in a similar role in the hospitality industry. Good level in English & Greek. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796431, 'Security Officer / Προσωπικό Ασφαλείας', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0nj9nnfrtmp4gpx2bpgjj8/security-officer--prosopiko-asfaleias-', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:24', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a  Security Officer  to join our Security team. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job: Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Security Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Security Officer is responsible for the safety and security of all guests, colleagues and visitors of Mandarin Oriental, and the protection of all hotel assets. The Security Officer reports to the Security Supervisor. As Security Officer, you will be responsible for the following duties: Conduct property patrols and periodic inspections as per hotel procedures. Maintain accurate key control and follow lost and found procedures. Monitor safety and security systems, including surveillance cameras. Control entry and exit at the main gate to ensure safety. Respond to emergencies as part of the Emergency Response Team. Complete incident reports and cooperate with authorities when necessary. As Security Officer, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Valid Greek security personnel work permit. Basic first aid knowledge will be considered a plus. Fluency in English and Greek. Computer literacy in MS Office. Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(796432, 'In Room Dining Head Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0ngss5fqqjmmnckc1fqjs4/in-room-dining-head-waiter', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:26', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an In Room Dining Head Waiter to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the In Room Dining Head Waiter is responsible to provide the highest level of service and professional excellence, being ever present in the operation, ensuring the highest standards and completely satisfying our guests during their meal experience. The In Room Dining Head Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As In Room Dining Head Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties: Ensure mise en place is prepared for efficient In Room Dining service. Have full knowledge of the menu, take orders professionally, and up-sell products. Handle billing, special requests, and guest complaints efficiently. Prioritize guest satisfaction, proactive communication, and workplace safety. Ensure cleanliness, order accuracy, and compliance with service standards. Maintain a professional appearance, uniform, and hygiene standards. As In Room Dining Head Waiter, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit Valid driving license. 2 years of F&B service experience, in a luxury hotel operation. Fluency in English Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant Uniform and laundry of uniform Private Medical Insurance We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
(796433, 'Pizza Chef De Partie', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0nh4td6b8mye9r84xvw88z/pizza-chef-de-partie', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:26', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Pizza Chef De Partie  to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Pizza Chef De Partie carries out kitchen duties whilst ensuring smooth, coordinated team effort in the kitchen, with a focus on pizza preparation and baking. The Chef De Partie reports to the Pizza Chef. As Pizza Chef De Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties Work closely with the Pizza Sapienza team on daily operations, ensuring consistent quality in pizza production, including dough preparation, fermentation, and baking. Prepare and cook pizzas following established recipes and standards, ensuring proper texture, flavor, and presentation. Ensure proper food handling, monitor raw food availability, and inspect incoming goods. Attend all training sessions and participate in special events, promotions, and demonstrations. Maintain a clean, presentable uniform and ensure personal hygiene. Inform the Executive Chef and Pizza Chef regarding operational issues. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Pizza Chef De Partie, we expect from you Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 3 years of culinary experience, with a focus on pizza or Italian cuisine. Good level in English or Greek.  Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Με φυσική παρουσία'),
(796434, 'Head Waiter', 'https://www.skywalker.gr/el/aggelia-ergasias/01kr0nedy4q5kzvst2gah99em4/head-waiter', 'n/a', '2026-05-07', '2026-05-07 08:00:28', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Head Waiter  to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Head Waiter provides the highest level of service and professional excellence, while being ever present in the outlet operation. The Head Waiter reports to the F&B Supervisor. As Head Waiter, you will be responsible for the following duties Provide respectful and generous service to both guests and colleagues. Follow all service steps thoroughly, requesting assistance promptly to avoid service delays. Manage the opening and closing of the outlet, including mise en place and setup. Maintain cleanliness in service and back-of-house areas. Attend pre-service