inary and Guest Experience teams to deliver bespoke dining moments and special events. Contribute to menu planning, seasonal concepts, and initiatives that drive revenue and enhance guest experience.   Requirements Previous experience in a luxury hotel, resort, or high-end restaurant in a supervisory or assistant management role. Strong understanding of fine dining service, wine service, and Mediterranean/Greek culinary culture. Degree or Diploma in Tourism or a related field. Excellent command of the English language; additional languages are considered an asset.   Candidate’s Profile: Strong leadership skills, problem-solving ability, and exceptional attention to detail. Flexibility to adapt to a variety of work situations and operational demands. Genuine passion for delivering exceptional levels of guest service. Benefits Staff accommodation, including Wi-Fi access and air conditioning. Half board meal plan (Breakfast, Lunch). Continuous training and development. Excellent career growth opportunities within the company or through other Marriott International hotels.     At Empiria Group we are proud to foster Equal Employment Opportunities regardless of race, color, ethnicity, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation.   You provide the talent as we flourish the skills to unleash your full career potential. Join our path of excellence!', 'Εποχιακή εργασία'),
